A||N||20||William||Dash trim preferences||||14||
Z||000000||William||01-09-2000||12:24 PM||||I'm thinking about trim choices today as my customizing continues. I currently have the brushed aluminum type dash trim, but it is not mint and I'll need to do something about it. I'm not sure if I want to find stock replacement parts or go aftermarket. I would like to have black formica type trim but no one makes it. Now I'm looking at REAL woodgrain type trim. I'm striving to make the fiero more exotic and not sure what type of trim would help with this. I'm afraid that the woodgrian trim might give the interior a fleetwood cadilac look.Any comments on this entire subject guys? Anyone know what type of dash trim is used in the Ferarri 308? I'd like to see a good thread on the subject.||||reg||14
Z||000001||deceler8||01-09-2000||01:04 PM||||If you want black trim, just sand the "aluminum" finish off your pieces...it's black plastic underneath, and if done properly, this black plastic will hold a high gloss.<P>I used a fine sanding sponge (3M) wet, and followed up with 400, 800 and 1500 grit wet paper to remove the scratches. Then I used  my Dremel with polishing compound and the parts shine and look like new.<P>I did this because my trim pieces were cracked and had the finish worn off them. I replaced them with junkyard pieces for $3 and they now all match and look great.||||reg||10
Z||000002||Monkeyman||01-09-2000||01:41 PM||||I was gonna suggest black Lexan or Plexiglass.  Would either of these give the dash more "depth" than just sanding off the stock finish?  Either of these are easy to work with and very forgiving.  I got a piece of scrap 26ga SS from work and thought about cutting it to fit the dash pieces, but it seems like more work than I want to do.  I was gonna have the shop (I work in a machine shop) punch the holes, etc, but they don't have a square punch with rounded corners.||||reg||1
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||01-09-2000||03:07 PM||||What would be nice is polished aluminum trim parts along with a aluminum/leather shift knob. They would be expensive though.||||reg||10
Z||000004||GREENDANO||01-09-2000||03:36 PM||||Try here for aluminum dash inserts<BR>----&gt; <A HREF="http://members.xoom.com/jrisagod/jrisagod.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.xoom.com/jrisagod/jrisagod.htm</A> ||||reg||1
