Z||000006||William||01-09-2000||06:06 PM||||The aluminum is interesting but think I would rather it be brushed. I'm afraid the billet may look too hot rodish and get away from the Exotic look I want. I'm redoing the entire interior in tan leather, and starting to think that a dark woodgrain might go well. I haven't seen many really dark kits tho. Ebony would really look good I think! Any one got the URL for Florida auto trim?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Bill Osmer||01-09-2000||06:47 PM||||William - (ahhh, my name sake...)<BR>I've gone thru the same thought process and investigated what was available via the i-net. I found some real wood dashes, but were not cheap. Finally found this (http://members.xoom.com/_XMCM/dlagrua/fierowooddash.htm) from Dennis Lagrua that is the right price and looks great. I've just ordered and expect deliver within the next week. I can let you know how it looks, but it will be my opinion.||||reg||1
Z||000008||DaRkLoRD||01-09-2000||07:24 PM||||How expensive are brushed aluminum panels anyway?<P>I'd either like brushed aluminum or carbon fiber, like DXR_DAD has. (I'll be posting a photo of it and some info on my site soon)||||reg||1
Z||000009||William||01-09-2000||07:49 PM||||Hmmmm.  I had rejected carbon fiber because I have never seen it in a exotic and not sure if it would look out of place. However, It is sort of black like I wanted with a little design that might be even better. That site that Bill listed even has a cheaper reproduction that would be fine if it looked like the real thing. Is DXR Dad's  real or the repoduction? Darklord, I would love to the  pic of it. Are there any other pics of CF fiero trim installed that I could be pointed to?||||reg||1
Z||000010||Monkeyman||01-09-2000||10:04 PM||||William-Carbon Fiber is very exotic (and very expensive).  Personally I don't care for the looks of it and would rather go with polished aluminum or SS.||||reg||1
